#: processes/review-task.bpmn:37
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The generic review position: classify what changed, descend into the review that fits it, consolidate what comes back, and accept or send back. You are in this process for any change under review. It is a DISPATCHER — the actor takes on the inner lane's role for the call path only — which is why prose and code can both be reviewed without either reviewer having to know the other's criteria. A change that is both goes through both. The accept-or-send-back decision lives here and nowhere beneath it. The subprocesses produce findings; this is the only lane entitled to turn findings into an outcome, and keeping that single makes \"who decided\" answerable."
msgstr ""
